From: ROCKNIX/DUCKTALE
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: pin protocol v1 (SM8750 ADSP contract)

Linux 7.1 introduced SMP2P v2 support and the AP now self-advertises v2
when the remote has not published a version yet. The SM8750 vendor ADSP
firmware (which owns the charger stack) was never validated against v2
negotiation. Two symptoms appeared with the 7.1 bump, both absent on
7.0.11 with identical firmware:

 - a permanent smp2p-adsp interrupt storm at runtime, and
 - a hard SoC wedge (forced-reset only) whenever a USB-C VBUS event
   (charger plug/unplug) arrives while the AP is in deep suspend: smp2p
   also carries the sleepstate signal that tells the ADSP the AP is
   asleep, and a broken contract leaves the fw handling the charger
   event against a wrong AP state. DPM-watchdog/SDAM forensics show the
   kernel never reaches a stuck device: the death is below the kernel.

Pin the negotiated version to 1, restoring the exact 7.0 semantics on
this platform.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -579,10 +579,12 @@ static int qcom_smp2p_alloc_outbound_item(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 	 * item by writing a valid version number.
 	 */
 	wmb();
-	if (in_version && in_version <= 2)
-		out->version = in_version;
-	else
-		out->version = 2;
+	/*
+	 * ROCKNIX: the SM8750 vendor ADSP was never validated against v2
+	 * negotiation (runtime irq storm + fw death on VBUS-in-suspend).
+	 * Keep the pre-7.1 contract.
+	 */
+	out->version = 1;
 
 	qcom_smp2p_kick(smp2p);
 
